    "warnings": [],
    "working_thesis": "Human action and speech, rooted in the human condition of plurality and natality, reveal unique individual identities and generate unpredictable, boundless processes and power, yet they suffer from inherent frailty and unpredictability which historical traditions have attempted to remedy through substitution (making/rulership) or which action natively redeems through the faculties of forgiving and promising."
